 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2017-10-31",
   "text": "Security and Financial Empowerment Act of 2017\n This bill sets forth various provisions to promote the safety and security of survivors of domestic violence, dating violence, sexual assault, and stalking,\n Among other things, the bill does the following:\n requires employers to provide up to 30 days of safe leave in a 12-month period; and \n prohibits states from imposing additional restrictions on eligibility for unemployment compensation."
  }
 ],
